1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:02,267
[HeyNavi] A cabinet is visible ahead on your left.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,300
Nobody asked. It noticed.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,267
HeyNavi is a walking companion for blind and low-vision people.

4
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:12,967
Most AI apps describe one photo when you ask.

5
00:00:12,967 --> 00:00:16,067
HeyNavi keeps watching, and speaks up when it matters.

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:21,433
[HeyNavi] I'm looking around. I'll tell you what I notice.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,700
[HeyNavi] A long empty hallway with doors on both sides.

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,167
Things in your way come first.

9
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:32,233
[HeyNavi] Possible obstacle: 2 tables directly ahead. 4 booth seats are visible ahead.

10
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:35,033
[HeyNavi] Stairwell with steps descending ahead.

11
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:37,567
The decision panel shows each look.

12
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:40,433
Steps again? Nothing new, so it stays quiet.

13
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Need the exit? Just ask.

14
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,400
[User] Where is the exit?

15
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,633
HeyNavi takes a fresh photo.

16
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:48,100
[HeyNavi] Let me look.

17
00:00:48,567 --> 00:00:51,067
[HeyNavi] An exit sign is ahead on your left near the ceiling.

18
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,267
Looking for a classroom? Ask which room it is.

19
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,033
[User] Which room is this?

20
00:00:56,067 --> 00:00:58,967
Muse Spark reads the sign in a fresh photo.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,067
[HeyNavi] Let me look.

22
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,533
[HeyNavi] This is the lactation room, directly ahead.

23
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:07,433
Or ask for the elevator.

24
00:01:07,667 --> 00:01:08,933
[User] Where's the elevator?

25
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:12,900
[HeyNavi] There are two elevators ahead on your left, next to each other.

26
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,167
SAM 3.1 outlines it.

27
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:19,367
Every few seconds, Muse Spark lists what matters for walking.

28
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:23,967
SAM 3.1 checks each item on the same frame and draws its box.

29
00:01:23,967 --> 00:01:28,033
Then HeyNavi decides: say it, hedge it, or stay quiet.

30
00:01:28,033 --> 00:01:30,233
And it never says a path is safe.

31
00:01:30,233 --> 00:01:33,800
Questions use the same loop: Spark answers from a fresh photo,

32
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,800
and SAM finds the thing and says where it is.

33
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:45,100
On our own test runs, a look takes about five seconds on the phone.

34
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,767
SAM confirmed 83% of what Spark proposed,

35
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:52,933
and a stop command cuts the voice in about 17 milliseconds.

36
00:01:57,667 --> 00:02:00,100
Signs, doors, things on the floor.

37
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,700
Visual information is everywhere,

38
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,933
and hard to reach without sight.

39
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:07,733
HeyNavi notices it, unasked, and answers when you ask.

40
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:13,933
HeyNavi doesn't replace a cane or a guide dog.

41
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:16,267
Walking navigation could come next.

42
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:18,933
Open source, built during this hackathon.
